TIKTOK DOOR AGENT — PROJECT NOTES
===================================

CONCEPT
- "Choose a Door" TikTok series — 2 posts/day, fully automated
- Viewer sees a PAST door and a FUTURE door, picks one in 3 seconds
- One door is good, one is bad (randomized each video)
- User-created intro video (3s) stitched with AI-generated reveals

PIPELINE
1. Script Generator  — Claude Haiku API writes narration + image prompts
2. Image Generator   — Flux Schnell (Replicate) generates door reveal images
3. TTS Generator     — Edge TTS (free) narrates each reveal
4. Video Assembler   — MoviePy/FFmpeg stitches intro + images + audio (1080x1920)
5. TikTok Uploader   — Content Posting API auto-uploads with caption/hashtags

BUDGET (target: £15/month)
- Claude Haiku API:     ~£0.50/mo
- Flux Schnell images:  ~£3-5/mo  (~120-240 images)
- Edge TTS:             FREE
- FFmpeg/MoviePy:       FREE
- TikTok API:           FREE
- Estimated total:      ~£4-6/mo

SETUP CHECKLIST
[ ] Run .\setup.bat (creates venv, installs deps, copies .env)
[ ] Add ANTHROPIC_API_KEY to .env (console.anthropic.com)
[ ] Add REPLICATE_API_TOKEN to .env (replicate.com/account/api-tokens)
[ ] Install FFmpeg (winget install FFmpeg)
[ ] Create intro video -> assets/intro.mp4 (3s, 1080x1920, two doors)
[ ] Apply for TikTok developer account (developers.tiktok.com)
[ ] Add TikTok credentials to .env once approved
[ ] Test with: python run.py

RUNNING
- Single video:   python run.py
- 2x daily:       python scheduler.py (posts at 09:00 and 19:00)
- Works without TikTok creds — just saves videos to output/ folder

FILES
assets/intro.mp4          — user-created intro clip (you make this)
output/                   — generated videos land here
src/config.py             — settings, API keys, video dimensions
src/script_generator.py   — LLM script generation
src/image_generator.py    — Flux image generation
src/tts_generator.py      — Edge TTS narration
src/video_assembler.py    — video stitching
src/tiktok_uploader.py    — TikTok Content Posting API
src/pipeline.py           — orchestrator (runs all 5 steps)
